From 4090f8ef3a2f4189fa348caa8cf8939bd49c94ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wintch <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:03:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] openxr_data: external recenter trigger file
 (XRIZER_RECENTER_FILE), polled from WaitGetPoses

A dashboard button (or any script) touches $HOME/vr/logs/xrizer-recenter
(override: $XRIZER_RECENTER_FILE); every ~30th WaitGetPoses -- for every
title, whether or not it ever asks for IVRInput -- looks for the file,
removes it and recenters BOTH play-space origins on the current head pose:
Standing keeps the floor height, Seated takes the head height, yaw only.
Stronger than SteamVR, which never moves Standing: at a booth the STAGE
origin is wherever the SLAM tracker happened to start the session, and the
title universe is not known here. For headset-only titles with no button to
hold for the held-menu shortcut (Dreams of Dali).

Guards: a trigger older than 10 s is discarded unused (a touch made with no
title running cannot recenter the next launch); a session that is not
FOCUSED leaves the file in place (Dali tears its bootstrap session down
~30 ms after the first frame); with XR_EXT_user_presence enabled a doffed
headset ignores it; and reset_tracking_space now refuses to anchor on a
head pose whose POSITION/ORIENTATION_VALID flags are unset (this also
covers the held-menu shortcut and ResetSeatedZeroPose).

Worn test 2026-08-29 (Dreams of Dali via the booth button): wearer turned
90 degrees left, operator pressed, the scene came round to the front; the
stale-trigger and FOCUSED paths logged as designed.
